====================================================================================================
(2) MASSIVE FLOW: entropic c_E(R) = 3 R S'(R) and Markov c_M(R) = -3R^2 S''(R)
    (Note 3, eqs. (cM), (cE)); staggered mass m, mu = m/2, xi = 2/m sites,
    RG variable mu R = m R/2.  PRIMARY DEFINITION c_M := c_M^(2) = 3R^2 I_{R-2}(2)/4,
    a genuine lattice CMI (>= 0 by SSA).  At a fixed point c_M^(d) =
    -(3R^2/d^2)log(1-d^2/R^2) = c(1 + d^2/2R^2 + ...), so c_M^(2) carries a known
    +2/R^2 bias; the Richardson column (4c_M^(2)-c_M^(4))/3 removes it in the UV
    but is INVALID once mu d >~ 1 (there I_{R-d}(d) is exponential in d, not
    polynomial) - it even goes negative in the deep IR and is shown for reference.
====================================================================================================

